# Formats and lints staged files, then re-stages whatever it fixed.
#
# Invoked bare rather than through yarn: husky puts node_modules/.bin on PATH,
# so this resolves to the project's own lint-staged regardless of which yarn or
# package manager happens to be active. `yarn lint-staged` would break for
# anyone whose global yarn is v1.
#
# lint-staged stashes unstaged hunks before running, so a file that is only
# partially staged is formatted from its staged content alone. Committing
# unstaged work by accident is the failure this prevents.
lint-staged
